{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/306321-hack-chimera-in-ctl","id":306321,"title":"Hack: Chimera in CtL","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-07T19:40:00-08:00","id":306321,"title":"Hack: Chimera in CtL","content":"The following is strictly a hack. Don\u2019t like it? Don\u2019t use it. <br /> <br /> The core premise here is that <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s Arcadia and <b>Mage</b>\u2019s are one and the same (or at least the same sort of thing). The twist is that I\u2019m referring to the upcoming <b>Mage 2e</b>\u2019s conception of Arcadia, where it is an overlay of wherever you happen to be. The protagonists look around them and see a landscape that resembles the home of the Gentry, with goblin-like creatures lurking in the shadows; look at them too closely, and they\u2019ll notice you. Mages call them Supernal Entities; we\u2019ll call them Chimerical Entities. These entities are normally only visible and able to interact with those who see them, though changelings have an ability to call upon their Wyrd to make such creatures manifest physically. When mortals witness Chimera that have manifested, two things happen: the chimera start to fall apart (an effect mages call Dissonance), and the witnesses forget what they saw (called Quiescence by mages, and the Mists by changelings). <br /> <br /> Changelings <i>also</i> have the ability to call on their Clarity to force a manifested chimerical being back into chimerical reality, or to drive it away; these options are similar to the \u201cabjuration\u201d options that all mortals can utilize against ephemeral beings, save only for the dice pool and the lack of any sort of ritual. So high-Wyrd changelings can bring Chimerical beings into material reality, and high-Clarity changelings can drive them away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T21:47:25-08:00","id":306406,"title":"","content":"What, like the beginning manifestations of their Arcadian Claiming?<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, I'm poking something hunter-esque in that direction. So, by all means, tell me more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}